 "notes": [
  "All FY figures taken from the registration document of that fiscal year (current-year column, as originally reported); EUR millions unless stated.",
  "Sign conventions: IS/CF/BS as printed (parentheses -> negative). memo.da_cf/da_fixed are positive (as printed in CF / note text); memo.impairment is the 'Impairment losses' line of the note 'Other income and expenses' with its printed (negative) sign.",
  "memo.da_fixed = 'Total depreciation and amortisation of tangible and intangible assets included in operating expenses (Other income and expenses and Cost of sales)' from the Other income and expenses note text (= CF D&A line). The note's 'Amortisation' line within Other income and expenses alone was 118.4 (2014), 147.3 (2015), 168.1 (2016), 167.1 (2017).",
  "2014-2017 CF statements show 'Impairment losses' as a separate line from 'Depreciation and amortisation' (22.7 / 27.9 / 30.3 / 41.9); cf.da excludes it; it is in cf_other.",
  "2016 impairment in OIE note per 2016 RD = (28.0); the 2017 RD comparative shows (30.3) for 2016 (reclassified with 'Other expenses' (15.1)->(12.9)). Original 2016 figure kept.",
  "CF 2014-2017 has no single 'Operating investments' line: cf.capex left null; components (Purchase of intangible assets, Purchase of PP&E) are in cf_other; apm.operating_investments is the 'Operating investments' figure from the MD&A investments table (2014 RD p.97 prints it rounded as 279; the 2015 RD restates it as 278.9) / segment note (2016-2017).",
  "Key figures 'Investments (excluding financial investments)' = operating investments + investments in financial assets (associates): 322.2 (2014), 266.6 (2015), 285.4 (2016), 270.1 (2017).",
  "cf.acq maps 'Investments in associates' (2014, 2016) / 'Investments in subsidiaries and associates' (2015, 2017). cf.d_inv_pay maps 'Amounts payable relating to fixed assets / to fixed asset suppliers'. cf.disp_cons (2016) = 'Proceeds from sale of investments in associates' 9.5.",
  "CF bridge: change in net cash = CFO + CFI + CFF + 'Change in scope' + 'Foreign currency translation adjustment on intra-group transactions' + 'Foreign currency translation adjustment'. Only the last is in cf.fx; the other two are in cf_other.",
  "BS: 'Investment property' (separate non-current asset line) is in bs_other; 'Financial instruments included in equity' (2014-2016) / 'Revaluation adjustments' (2017) mapped to reval_adj. equity_parent is not a separate line on the face of the BS: taken from the statement of changes in equity / key figures (3,449.0 / 3,742.0 / 4,382.6 / 5,039.0). Actuarial gains/losses are included within 'Reserves' on the BS face.",
  "BS cash ('Cash and cash equivalents') differs slightly from note 19 sub-total (e.g. 2014: 1,441.6 vs 1,443.3); net cash position (CF end) = cash and equivalents less bank overdrafts per note 19.",
  "2015 reclassification: from 2015 the annual free-share plan (IFRS 2) expense (36.4 in 2015) is recognised in 'Other income and expenses' instead of 'Selling, marketing and administrative expenses'. 2014 as originally reported keeps it in SG&A; 2015 RD note 5/6 states 2014 pro forma would be SG&A (1,253.2) and OIE (200.5) (not restated in the 2015 IS comparative). 2015 RD p.188.",
  "Segment note: ROI by area = segment 'Operating income'/'Operating result'; 'Holding' column mapped to roi_unalloc. Revenue by destination.",
  "Sector table: 2014 RD notes that 'Tableware' is henceforth presented in 'Other Hermes business lines' (La Table Hermes) and 'Other products' (Saint-Louis, Puiforcat), applied retrospectively (2014 RD note 3.2). Sector values from the consolidated note 3.2 (one decimal); constant-currency growth from the management report tables (rounded to 0.1%).",
  "Exceptional dividends: EUR 5.00 per share extraordinary dividend in respect of FY2014 (proposed to AGM 2 June 2015, paid 2015, total ~EUR 522m paid in 2015) and EUR 5.00 per share exceptional dividend in respect of FY2017 (proposed to AGM 5 June 2018). dps_exceptional is recorded against the fiscal year in respect of which it was declared (2014 and 2017).",
  "French taxes: the 10.7% exceptional CIT surcharge applied 2011-2015 (French rate 38.0% in 2014-2015; removed in 2016, rate 34.43%) - its amount is not disclosed, so excep_tax is null for 2014-2016. The 3% tax on dividends distributed was included in income tax: EUR 8.9m (2014), EUR 25.0m (2015), EUR 10.5m (2016) (tax notes 8.2).",
  "2017 (RD 2017 note 8.2 p.211): the French Constitutional Council invalidated the 3% dividend tax in Oct 2017; the two exceptional contributions of 15% each due in France in 2017, net of the reimbursement receivable of the 3% dividend tax, represent a net expense of EUR 20 million -> memo.excep_tax = 20 (net expense). Gross amounts not disclosed; no 'net income excluding' figure published.",
  "Restated net cash: 2014-2016 definition 'includes non-liquid financial investments and borrowings'; 2017 RD redefines it as including cash investments that do not meet IFRS cash-equivalent criteria (original maturity > 3 months). No reconciliation table printed, so cash_inv_gt3m/fin_liab_restated are null. 2017 non-current financial assets jumped to 270.9 (purchase of other financial assets 142.7).",
  "No 'Adjusted free cash flow' APM was published for 2014-2017 (adj_fcf null).",
  "Treasury shares: number held per consolidated note 20 (2014: 1,167,264; 2015: 1,180,771; 2016: 1,079,660; 2017: 1,415,702). Share capital: 105,569,412 shares of EUR 0.51 each throughout.",
  "Quarterly Q4 revenue from revenue releases: Q4/15 (2016-02-09 release), Q4/16 (2017-02-07 release and 2016 results release), Q4/17 (2018-02-07 release and 2017 results release). Q4/14 not extracted (no FY2014 quarterly release in source set).",
  "IS label: 'Current operating income' in the 2015 RD = Recurring operating income. Pre-tax income label 'Net income before tax' (2016-2017). 2016 and 2017 IS: no nonrec items (line printed as '-')."
